BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-10-09-computational-phenotypes@edm-megalab.emory.edu
DTSTAMP:20261020T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T133000
SUMMARY:Computational phenotypes: traits\, states\, or moving targets? — 
 Emory Decision-Making Megalab
DESCRIPTION:Article discussion. At our September 25 meeting\, we discusse
 d individual differences\, repeated measurement\, parameter stability\, 
 and what makes a useful computational phenotype\, drawing on Schurr et a
 l. (2024) and the companion paper by Katahira\, Oba & Toyama (2024). Fea
 tured article: Dynamic computational phenotyping of human cognition. Aut
 hors: Schurr\, Reznik\, Hillman\, Bhui\, et al.. Journal: Nature Human B
 ehaviour (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-024-01814-x Featured art
 icle: Does the reliability of computational models truly improve with hi
 erarchical modeling? Some recommendations and considerations for the ass
 essment of model parameter reliability. Authors: Katahira\, Oba & Toyama
 . Journal: Psychonomic Bulletin & Review (2024). https://doi.org/10.3758
 /s13423-024-02490-8 Lead: Michael Hallquist. Location: PAIS 280.
LOCATION:PAIS 280
URL:https://hallquistlab.github.io/edm_megalab/meetings/2026-09-25-comput
 ational-phenotypes/
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-11-community-kickoff@edm-megalab.emory.edu
DTSTAMP:20261020T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T133000
SUMMARY:What should EDM Megalab be? — Emory Decision-Making Megalab
DESCRIPTION:Community planning meeting. Everyone in the Emory community w
 ith an interest in decision-making is welcome. Building on the broad par
 ticipation at our September 25 meeting\, we will get to know one another
 \, map shared interests\, methods\, datasets\, and opportunities\, and s
 hape priorities for the series. Join the conversation whether you attend
 ed last time or are new to EDM Megalab.  Lead: Michael Hallquist. Locati
 on: PAIS 280.
LOCATION:PAIS 280
URL:https://hallquistlab.github.io/edm_megalab/meetings/2026-10-09-commun
 ity-planning/
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
